            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0778" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg764"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ashton, Acting
                        Attorney-General, to Mr. Seward, Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office of the
                            Attorney-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-09"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 9, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[11]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your
                    communication of the 2d instant, inclosing a copy of a note of the 20th ultimo,
                    addressed to you by the minister of Spain, relative to a supposed intended
                    violation of the neutrality laws at New Orleans, was duly received at this
                    office.</p>
                <p>The inclosure was at once forwarded to the United States attorney at New Orleans,
                    with instructions to institute inquiry as to the truth of the allegations
                    contained in Mr. Tassara’s note, and to take such legal measures as might be
                    found necessary and proper in the premises.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUBLEY ASHTON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                            Attorney-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
